            },
            "createdOn": 1780471256,
            "author": {
                "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                "username": "Vijaysankarr"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Isn't this error thrown already by systemd?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "from what I can see, systemd/sd-bus does throw org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.ObjectPathInUse when a vtable is registered at an already-taken D-Bus path. \nBut in phosphor-snmp, the object paths use an incrementing ID (lastClientId++), not something derived from address+port, so even duplicate clients would end up with different paths like /xyz/.../1, /xyz/.../2, and sd-bus would never detect the conflict.\n\nThe duplicate detection here is application-level logic (same address+port already configured), which sd-bus has no way to enforce on its own. That's the gap this error is meant to fill."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "This detail needs to go to the commit message and/or description to distinguish object vs path. Also, which path do we log in the error - the existing one?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "@deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com,\n\nUpdated the commit message.\nOnce this merges, I'll raise the follow-on patch in phosphor-snmp to use this error and pass the existing client's path."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ratan Gupta",
                        "email": "ratankgupta31@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ratagupt"
                    },
                    "message": ">so even duplicate clients would end up with different paths like /xyz/.../1, /xyz/.../2, and sd-bus would never detect the conflict.\n\nThat is not correct. Please check the implementation here:\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-snmp/blob/master/snmp_conf_manager.cpp#L37C5-L37C26\n\nThe code already checks for duplicate clients before creating a new object, so the scenario of duplicate clients ending up with different object paths does not apply.\n\nInstead, you could say that the current implementation throws an InvalidArgument error when a duplicate client is detected, and your proposed change is to return ObjectAlreadyExists"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "You're right,\nthe current implementation throws an InvalidArgument error when a duplicate client is detected, and proposed change is to return ObjectAlreadyExists as mentioned in the TODO.\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-snmp/blob/d6c5bef671991809ddd37089aeb47f68590fb09f/snmp_conf_manager.cpp#L83\n\nI mentioned the incrementing ID detail while explaining the distinction from systemd's ObjectPathInUse and it came across wrong."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "@patrick@stwcx.xyz / @ratankgupta31@gmail.com\ncould you review this patch ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "@deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com,\ncould you review this patch?"
                }
            ],
