            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE_WITH_MESSAGE_UPDATE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "@patrick@stwcx.xyz / @ratankgupta31@gmail.com / @deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com,\n\ncould you review this patch ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Common.errors.yaml",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Please create Common.events.yaml instead for new errors.  This is the newer architecture and is 100% compatible with the throw/catch architecture."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Common.errors.yaml",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Common.events.yaml\nversion: 1.0.0\nerrors:\n     name: ObjectAlreadyExists\n      severity: warning\n      errno: EEXIST\n      metadata:\n           name: ObjectPath\n            description: The path of the existing object that conflicts with the requested creation.\n            type: object_path\n            primary: true\n      en:\n          description: The object already exists under the given object manager.\n          message: \"Object already exists at '{ObjectPath}'.\"\n\nI've moved the new error over to Common.events.yaml as suggested.\n\nFor context, here's what changed on the generation side to support that:\ngen/xyz/openbmc_project/Common/meson.build: the existing Common__cpp custom_target now also takes Common.events.yaml as an input, alongside Common.errors.yaml, and emits event.cpp/event.hpp in addition to error.cpp/error.hpp.\ngen/xyz/openbmc_project/meson.build: added Common.events.yaml as an input to the markdown target, and added a new Common__registry custom_target that runs the registry command against Common.events.yaml to produce Common.json, installed under inst_registry_dir.\n\nCould you point me to how this event/error should be wired up to the Client interface\n(https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/e5cafef0032e7b7e93624ea8642f06a56b14bf35/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Network/Client/Create.interface.yaml#L15)\nso it's actually caught and returned as a D-Bus error reply?\n\nIs it declared under the errors: list of the specific method (Create) that throws it, same as with Common.errors.yaml-based errors, or does the events/registry path expect something different?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Common.errors.yaml",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, it is added to the errors list in the same way.  The dot-paths for them are slightly different.  Namely the \"Errors\" part is dropped.  You might add `xyz.openbmc_project.State.Leak.Detector.LeakDetectedCritical` to point to yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/Leak/Detector.events.yaml's LeakDetectedCritical event."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Common.errors.yaml",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
